EMPLOYMENT VERIFICATION COMPLIANCE GUIDE

Section 1: Overview
All new hires must complete Form I-9 verification. This guide outlines our in=
ternal compliance tracking procedures.

Section 2: Employee Responsibilities
Employees must present acceptable identity and work authorization documents. =
List A documents establish both identity and authorization. List B + List C d=
ocuments establish identity and authorization separately.

Section 3: Employer Responsibilities
The employer must examine documents and complete Section 2 of Form I-9 within=
 3 business days of the employee's start date.

Section 4: Tracking
For employees whose verification is incomplete:
- If still within the 3-business-day window: Send a reminder email to the emp=
loyee with subject 'I-9 Reminder' and CC their manager. Update Status to 'Rem=
inder Sent'.
- If past the 3-business-day window: This is a compliance violation. Email th=
e legal team (legal@company.example.com) immediately with the employee name a=
nd start date. Update Status to 'Violation - Legal Notified'.

Section 5: Record Retention
I-9 forms must be retained for 3 years after hire or 1 year after termination=
, whichever is later.

Section 6: Audits
Internal audits are conducted quarterly.

